mt76: backport upstream e59324380042 "wifi: mt76: fix HE DCM max-RU capability encoding"

Upstream commit e59324380042cb2f0a6ab0405f5950ffead97003 (Felix Fietkau,
2026-07-02, on mt76 master; not an ancestor of the 39c960c3 pin that
OpenWrt 25.12.5 and MediaTek's 25.12 feed both ship):

    sta_rec_he.dcm_rx_max_nss was assigned twice: the second assignment,
    sourced from HE PHY capability byte 8 (DCM max RU), overwrote the
    RX-NSS value and left dcm_max_ru at zero.  Every associated HE station
    advertising DCM support was configured in firmware with a wrong
    dcm_rx_max_nss and a zero dcm_max_ru.

    Fixes: c336318f57a9 ("mt76: mt7915: add HE capabilities support for peers")
    Fixes: 67aa27431c7f ("mt76: mt7921: rely on mt76_connac_mcu common library")

Carried in the CR6608 MURU series because the HE station record is the
firmware's per-peer input for trigger MCS selection; it is a correctness
fix for DCM-capable peers, not a scheduler policy change.

diff --git a/mt76_connac_mcu.c b/mt76_connac_mcu.c
index 89bd52ea..a515b09e 100644
--- a/mt76_connac_mcu.c
+++ b/mt76_connac_mcu.c
@@ -748,7 +748,7 @@ mt76_connac_mcu_sta_he_tlv(struct sk_buff *skb, struct ieee80211_sta *sta)
 		HE_PHY(CAP3_DCM_MAX_CONST_RX_MASK, elem->phy_cap_info[3]);
 	he->dcm_rx_max_nss =
 		HE_PHY(CAP3_DCM_MAX_RX_NSS_2, elem->phy_cap_info[3]);
-	he->dcm_rx_max_nss =
+	he->dcm_max_ru =
 		HE_PHY(CAP8_DCM_MAX_RU_MASK, elem->phy_cap_info[8]);
 
 	he->pkt_ext = 2;
diff --git a/mt7915/mcu.c b/mt7915/mcu.c
index 202d8ac4..a3a841a5 100644
--- a/mt7915/mcu.c
+++ b/mt7915/mcu.c
@@ -1224,7 +1224,7 @@ mt7915_mcu_sta_he_tlv(struct sk_buff *skb, struct ieee80211_sta *sta,
 		HE_PHY(CAP3_DCM_MAX_CONST_RX_MASK, elem->phy_cap_info[3]);
 	he->dcm_rx_max_nss =
 		HE_PHY(CAP3_DCM_MAX_RX_NSS_2, elem->phy_cap_info[3]);
-	he->dcm_rx_max_nss =
+	he->dcm_max_ru =
 		HE_PHY(CAP8_DCM_MAX_RU_MASK, elem->phy_cap_info[8]);
 
 	he->pkt_ext = 2;
